<v Boy>You know what people do?
<v Boy>你知道人们做什么吗？

00:58:37.200 --> 00:58:38.100
<v Brishun Gary>Shhh. I'm talking.
<v Brishun Gary>嘘。我在说话。

00:58:38.100 --> 00:58:38.860
<v Boy>Come on, man.
<v Boy>来吧，伙计。

00:58:38.860 --> 00:58:47.930
<v Brishun Gary>I just turn on the TV, do a search, and I type in Hurricane Season -- you know the movie that they made about New Orleans, yeah? I'll be watching that.
<v Brishun Gary>我只是打开电视，搜索，输入《Hurricane Season》——你知道他们拍的关于新奥尔良的电影吧？我就看那个。

00:58:47.930 --> 00:59:09.600
<v Ira Glass>Brishun Gary and his buddies talked to Zoe. They are 14, 13, and 11. And they do not remember the storm. Their big source of information, this film Hurricane Season , is a straight to DVD film about high school basketball players in the city after the storm. Needless to say, when these guys tell the story of the storm that destroyed their own neighborhood, it is without the pain you hear when adults tell it.
<v Ira Glass>Brishun Gary和他的伙计们和Zoe谈了话。他们14、13和11岁。他们不记得飓风了。他们信息的主要来源，这部电影《Hurricane Season》，是一部关于飓风后城市高中篮球运动员的直发DVD电影。不用说，当这些家伙讲述摧毁他们自己社区的飓风故事时，那是不带成年人讲述时听到的痛苦的。

00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:18.080
<v Brishun Gary>Because my grandmother was with that. They was living through that. She said they lying down. Next thing you know, all you hear was, ah, ah, swish.
<v Brishun Gary>因为我祖母经历过那个。他们经历了那个。她说他们躺着。接下来你知道的，你听到的全是，啊，啊，唰。

