00:59:59.010 --> 01:00:16.390
<v Breyana>Because I remember getting to spend time with my family. Because usually, you know your mom goes to work, and your grandma goes to work. And I was happy, because my mom and my grandma was at home, and we get to have fun with each other.
<v Breyana>因为我记得我得到了和家人在一起的时间。因为通常，你知道你妈妈去上班，你祖母去上班。我很高兴，因为我妈妈和祖母在家，我们能在一起玩得很开心。

01:00:16.390 --> 01:00:28.860
<v Bron>Like after Hurricane Katrina, we went from Mississippi, from Mississippi to Georgia, from Georgia to South Carolina, from South Carolina to North Carolina to North Carolina, Pennsylvania. I've been all over. [LAUGHS] I've been all over for real.
<v Bron>就像卡特里娜飓风后，我们去了密西西比，从密西西比去了佐治亚，从佐治亚去了南卡罗来纳，从南卡罗来纳去了北卡罗来纳，宾夕法尼亚。我到处都去过。（笑）我到处都去过，真的。

01:00:28.860 --> 01:00:32.410
<v Ira Glass>Bron was 12 when the storm hit and his family went all over.
<v Ira Glass>Bron在飓风来袭时12岁，他的家人到处走。

01:00:32.410 --> 01:00:45.420
<v Bron>It's pretty nice to actually see other states than just New Orleans. Because when I was young, I didn't used to see nothing else outside. Hurricane Katrina really helped me out to see other places. Yeah.
<v Bron>能看到新奥尔良以外的其他州真的挺不错的。因为当我小的时候，我过去什么都看不到。卡特里娜飓风真的帮我走出去看到了其他地方。是的。

01:00:45.420 --> 01:01:03.900
<v Ira Glass>Over on Gordon Street, between Burgundy and Rampart, Robyn ran into this 23-year-old, just, you know, on the street. And they started talking. And his name is Terrence Marshall. He went to Texas for a year after the storm. And then his family came back. And since then, he's found all of his old friends from when he was a little kid growing up here, from back when he was 13, except one of them.
<v Ira Glass>在Burgundy街和Rampart街之间的戈登街上，Robyn在街上遇到了这个23岁的年轻人。他们开始聊天。他叫Terrence Marshall。飓风后他在德克萨斯州待了一年。然后他的家人回来了。从那时起，他找到了他小时候在这里长大的所有老朋友，从他13岁时算起，除了其中一个。

01:01:03.900 --> 01:01:06.870
<v Terrence Marshall>His name's Samuel. Samuel.
<v Terrence Marshall>他叫Samuel。Samuel。

