01:04:04.270 --> 01:04:20.850
<v Terrence Marshall>Hey, I don't mean to cut you off. Not to cut you off, but you still talk-- like, you got a different accent. But you're still talking and responding the same way from when you were a little kid, son. You were like, uh. And you still do that.
<v Terrence Marshall>嘿，我不是故意打断你。不是要打断你，但你依然说话——你有不同的口音。但你说话和回应的方式和你小时候一模一样，孩子。你过去常说，呃。你现在依然这样做。

01:04:20.850 --> 01:04:25.750
<v Samuel>Yeah. They say I have like a dad laugh. That's how they made fun of me here.
<v Samuel>是的。他们说我有一种爸爸式的笑声。那就是他们在这里取笑我的方式。

01:04:25.750 --> 01:04:48.070
<v Terrence Marshall>[LAUGHS] Man, I'm not even gonna lie, man. I got a huge burden-- like, this is like a real-- I really feel like you blessed me just now. Like, seriously, it feel good. It feel real good talking to you son, because you were like my best friend, son. Like damn, dude.
<v Terrence Marshall>（笑）伙计，我甚至不想装模作样，伙计。我背负着巨大的负担——就像这是真实的——我觉得你刚才祝福了我。就像，认真地说，这感觉很好。和你谈话感觉真好，孩子，因为你就像我最好的朋友，孩子。该死，伙计。

01:04:48.070 --> 01:04:48.500
<v Samuel>Yeah.
<v Samuel>是的。

01:04:48.500 --> 01:06:06.300
<v Terrence Marshall>This feel good. This feel good talking to you. I ain't even going to front.
<v Terrence Marshall>这种感觉真好。和你谈话感觉真好。我甚至不想装。

